findings:
  - id: AOOSR-R5-IR-B01
    severity: blocker
    title: The fixed R4 disposition authority input is a malformed patch-contaminated file
    contract_surface:
      - control-plane/registry/reviews/2026-07-25-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r4-independent-review-disposition-v0.1.yaml
      - control-plane/registry/decisions/2026-07-25-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5-evidence-consumption-rebaseline-start-decision-v0.1.yaml
      - control-plane/registry/reports/2026-07-25-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5-atomic-independent-review-package-v0.1.manifest.yaml
    evidence: >-
      The fixed disposition has a valid-looking 2754-byte YAML prefix, followed
      by a literal "*** Add File:" patch marker and the complete 3327-byte
      active-work-queue-v18.9 document. The appended suffix is byte-equal to
      the separately stored queue. PyYAML rejects the fixed authority input
      with ScannerError. The bad bytes are identically present in the R5 ZIP
      and match the declared SHA-256, so this is a fixed semantic defect rather
      than transport corruption.
    impact: >-
      R5 cannot atomically consume the R4 finding disposition as a valid
      governance record. Hash equality proves only that the malformed bytes
      were reproduced; it does not establish the disposition semantics claimed
      by the R5 start decision and author self-review.
    required_disposition:
      - preserve_the_malformed_fixed_bytes_as_historical_evidence
      - create_a_clean_superseding_R4_disposition_correction_record
      - obtain_any_new_Jenn_scope_or_start_decision_needed_to_bind_the_superseding_record
      - rebuild_and_freshly_review_a_successor_atomic_bundle

  - id: AOOSR-R5-IR-B02
    severity: blocker
    title: The R5 validator accepts fully re-signed forbidden source mutations
    contract_surface:
      - control-plane/registry/drafts/2026-07-25-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5-evidence-consumption-rebaseline-v0.1.md
      - control-plane/registry/validate-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5.py
      - control-plane/registry/run-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5.py
    evidence: >-
      An independent temporary runner mutation inserted an uncounted
      "git cat-file -p SEALED_TREE" operation inside _run_exact_inventory.
      A second mutation invoked dynamic exec through getattr(builtins,
      "ex" + "ec") inside run_actual. Neither branch was executed during the
      probes. After updating the runner SHA-256 in an otherwise exact manifest,
      the R5 manifest parser accepted both records and the R5 validator returned
      no source-totality or semantic errors for either mutation.
    impact: >-
      The validator does not establish required proof items 3, 4 and 8 for a
      fully re-signed bundle. It can certify a successor source that performs
      an uncounted generic tree read or restores dynamic execution while the
      synthetic command inventory still claims exactly 23 operations.
    required_disposition:
      - make_source_totality_enforcement_structural_and_fail_closed_for_all_process_and_dynamic_execution_surfaces
      - prove_every_Git_subprocess_is_derived_from_one_exact_declarative_23_operation_plan
      - add_integrated_fully_resigned_runner_and_manifest_mutation_tests
      - require_target_semantic_rejections_for_obfuscated_dynamic_execution_and_uncounted_Git_operations

  - id: AOOSR-R5-IR-M01
    severity: major
    title: The receipt attributes an inventory fingerprint to an upstream source that does not define it
    contract_surface:
      - control-plane/registry/receipts/2026-07-24-yellow-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-execution-admission-materialization-preflight-v0.1.md
      - control-plane/registry/drafts/2026-07-24-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-protected-source-boundary-closure-v0.1-r1.md
      - control-plane/registry/drafts/2026-07-25-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5-evidence-consumption-rebaseline-v0.1.md
      - control-plane/registry/run-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r5.py
    evidence: >-
      The fixed upstream receipt contains the seven ordered protected path
      names but no protected_name_inventory_sha256 or canonical digest-preimage
      rule. The frozen Protected Source Boundary contract and freeze decision
      likewise do not state the digest. R5 nevertheless projects
      52349f79221f041a48134331666315686ed6185b0838c56c13b1e9ed3b247011
      as a consumed frozen upstream fact. That value can be reproduced only
      after independently choosing the newline-delimited ordered-name preimage,
      a rule not defined by the cited R5 upstream source_ref.
    impact: >-
      The digest value is reproducible but its claimed provenance is not
      self-describing or fully bound. A receipt consumer cannot distinguish an
      upstream-frozen fingerprint from a new R5 canonicalization convention.
    required_disposition:
      - either_remove_the_unowned_digest_claim_and_bind_only_the_exact_frozen_source
      - or_bind_a_superseding_frozen_upstream_record_that_defines_the_exact_order_encoding_and_SHA256_preimage
      - keep_observed_this_run_false_and_do_not_reintroduce_tree_enumeration_or_policy_recomputation

